":"U_kgDOBe5tvQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99511741?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction","html_url":"https://github.com/HolonProduction","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-11T16:47:14Z","updated_at":"2025-06-11T16:47:14Z","body":"> CC @HolonProduction as this seems LSP related.\r\n\r\nThe fact that the LSP runs every string through this, could probably be improved given that we have more fine grained knowledge about were a path is expected in the completion context, but it would require an architecture change to have this info available outside of completion.\r\n\r\nEven if we'd do that, we'd still need a way to resolve the path, which fails silently, since even if a path is expected there could be a user error. So having this fail silently (or providing a silent alternative) seems necessary to me. Can't say anything about this specific implementation though.\r\n\r\nAlso a learning from the current situation of `Variant::get` and typed dictionaries: if we make this fail silently, please add a documentation comment to make this contract explicit! Otherwise we'll just get regressions in the future because this behavior changes.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"